  "identifier": "bioformats",
  "name": "Bio-Formats",
  "description": "Java library for reading and writing life sciences image file formats, developed by the Open Microscopy Environment (OME) consortium. Supports 150+ proprietary and open microscopy formats including SVS, NDPI, SCN, CZI, LIF, ND2, MRXS, OME-TIFF, and DICOM and converts them to the OME data model and OME-TIFF standard. The foundational image I/O layer for QuPath, ImageJ/FIJI, OMERO, and most other bioimage analysis tools. GPL-2.0, 419 stars, v8.5.0 (March 2026), 22,000+ commits reflecting 20+ years of active development. Maintained by the OME consortium (University of Dundee, EMBL-EBI, and others).",
  "url": "https://www.openmicroscopy.org/bio-formats/",
  "codeRepository": "https://github.com/ome/bioformats",
